Mark XXV: the Portal speaks

The XR room was the last surface running a stripped conversation-only
chat. It now runs the SAME agent as every other body - the last holdout
falls, and all six surfaces share one brain, one gate, one stream.

- portal.py: PortalState is now a BridgeState subclass (the Mark IX
  machinery wearing the portal's token gate): full 24-tool agent,
  worker-thread turns, the event stream, and confirmations. New
  endpoints: GET /api/events (bounded long-poll), POST /api/confirm;
  POST /api/chat is now async (started / 409 busy). The plain-chat
  history and SYSTEM_PROMPT are gone - the Agent composes the persona.
- portal_page.py: the canvas chat panel renders the event stream -
  "..." placeholder cleared on the first event, YOU lines from user
  events, a growing "J: ... ▌" line for partials finalized by the reply,
  status lines, and an in-room APPROVE/DENY confirmation banner (DOM
  Overlay, visible in-headset). Replies are spoken as before; errors
  are not.
- Tests: portal round-trip now exercises the async turn - partials
  stream, the final reply matches, page carries the event/confirm/
  partial hooks. Board and models checks unchanged.
- Version 3.12.0.
